1
00:00:01,435 --> 00:00:04,772
♪ In the
not-too-distant future ♪

2
00:00:04,772 --> 00:00:08,042
♪ Somewhere in time and space ♪

3
00:00:08,042 --> 00:00:11,078
♪ Mike Nelson and
his robot pals ♪

4
00:00:11,078 --> 00:00:14,182
♪ Are caught in a nasty place ♪

5
00:00:14,182 --> 00:00:17,018
♪ They try to survive
the wrath of Pearl ♪

6
00:00:17,018 --> 00:00:20,188
♪ Just an evil gal who
wants to rule the world ♪

7
00:00:20,188 --> 00:00:23,190
♪ From her castle below,
she sets her sights above ♪

8
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:26,962
♪ Just to torture all
her captives on the
Satellite of Love ♪

9
00:00:26,962 --> 00:00:28,730
- [Mike] Get me down!

10
00:00:29,797 --> 00:00:32,867
♪ I'll send him cheesy movies ♪

11
00:00:32,867 --> 00:00:35,137
♪ The worst I can find ♪

12
00:00:35,137 --> 00:00:36,470
♪ La la la ♪

13
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,973
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

14
00:00:38,973 --> 00:00:41,475
♪ And I'll monitor his mind ♪

15
00:00:41,475 --> 00:00:42,810
♪ La la la ♪

16
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:45,213
♪ Now keep in mind
Mike can't control ♪

17
00:00:45,213 --> 00:00:47,615
♪ Where the movies
begin or end ♪

18
00:00:47,615 --> 00:00:48,617
♪ La la la ♪

19
00:00:48,617 --> 00:00:51,318
♪ He'll try to keep his sanity ♪

20
00:00:51,318 --> 00:00:56,290
♪ With the help of
his robot friends ♪

21
00:00:57,092 --> 00:00:58,125
♪ Robot roll call ♪

22
00:00:58,125 --> 00:00:59,560
♪ Cambot ♪
- You're on!

23
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:00,928
♪ Gypsy ♪
- Oh my stars!

24
00:01:00,928 --> 00:01:02,530
♪ Tom Servo ♪
- Check me out!

25
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:04,032
♪ Croooow ♪
- I'm different!

26
00:01:04,032 --> 00:01:07,202
♪ If you're wondering how
he eats and breathes ♪

27
00:01:07,202 --> 00:01:09,370
♪ And other science facts ♪

28
00:01:09,370 --> 00:01:10,838
♪ La la la ♪

29
00:01:10,838 --> 00:01:13,207
♪ Just repeat to yourself,
it's just a show ♪

30
00:01:13,207 --> 00:01:16,343
♪ I should really just relax ♪

31
00:01:16,343 --> 00:01:21,315
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000 ♪

32
00:01:21,315 --> 00:01:23,417
(guitar twanging)

33
00:01:23,417 --> 00:01:28,422
(mechanical whirring)
(doors closing)

34
00:01:34,928 --> 00:01:37,098
(humming)

35
00:01:38,533 --> 00:01:41,168
- Oh hey Mike, I see you've
got today's Boston Globe.

36
00:01:41,168 --> 00:01:42,437
- Yeah, Crow.

37
00:01:42,437 --> 00:01:44,205
I didn't know you had
a syndicated column

38
00:01:44,205 --> 00:01:47,542
in the lifestyle section
of many major newspapers.

39
00:01:47,542 --> 00:01:49,043
- Oh sure.

40
00:01:49,043 --> 00:01:51,880
I was inspired by Larry
King's column in USA Today.

41
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:54,282
- "My Two Cents,"
by Crow T. Robot.

42
00:01:54,282 --> 00:01:55,550
- Yeah.

43
00:01:55,550 --> 00:01:56,750
- "I said it before
and I'll say it again.

44
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:59,087
Shoelaces are handy,
even necessary

45
00:01:59,087 --> 00:02:00,722
to many of today's shoe styles."

46
00:02:00,722 --> 00:02:01,923
- Yeah.

47
00:02:01,923 --> 00:02:03,390
- "Volleyball player
Gabrielle Reece

48
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:05,025
is the best athlete in
the world, in arguably

49
00:02:05,025 --> 00:02:07,528
the most difficult
of all sports."

50
00:02:07,528 --> 00:02:08,997
- Right.

51
00:02:08,997 --> 00:02:12,533
- "The Boeing 727 is still
my favorite aircraft.

52
00:02:12,533 --> 00:02:15,770
I give Supreme Court Justice
Antonin Scalia a B-plus."

53
00:02:15,770 --> 00:02:17,038
- Yup.

54
00:02:17,038 --> 00:02:18,372
- "Television shows
aired last night."

55
00:02:18,372 --> 00:02:20,040
Crow, I have to say, this column

56
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,543
doesn't seem
particularly substantive.

57
00:02:22,543 --> 00:02:24,145
- Oh, thanks Mike.

58
00:02:24,145 --> 00:02:25,747
You should have seen
last Tuesday's column.

59
00:02:25,747 --> 00:02:27,582
I remarked on a patty
melt I had for lunch.

60
00:02:27,582 --> 00:02:29,050
- That's fascinating.

61
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:31,118
Now who reads this column?

62
00:02:31,118 --> 00:02:33,220
- Well, you for one.

63
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:36,257
- Crow, you are right
on about shoelaces, man.

64
00:02:36,257 --> 00:02:37,492
I don't know what
we'd do without

65
00:02:37,492 --> 00:02:39,893
journalists like you
telling it like it is.

66
00:02:39,893 --> 00:02:41,195
- We'll be right back.

67
00:02:41,195 --> 00:02:44,965
- Wow, television shows
did air last night!

68
00:02:44,965 --> 00:02:48,570
(instrumental theme music)

69
00:02:51,005 --> 00:02:53,273
- Okay Mike, is this
more substantial?

70
00:02:53,273 --> 00:02:56,912
Could there be more goose
poop in my front yard?

71
00:02:56,912 --> 00:02:58,245
- No.

72
00:02:58,245 --> 00:02:59,780
- No, it's not more substantial,

73
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:02,017
or no, there could not be
more goose poop in my...

74
00:03:02,017 --> 00:03:03,852
- Let's see what
Pearl's up to, okay?

75
00:03:03,852 --> 00:03:06,387
- I just wanted an answer.

76
00:03:06,387 --> 00:03:09,323
(thunder crashing)

77
00:03:11,993 --> 00:03:13,862
- Huh?
- What the?

78
00:03:13,862 --> 00:03:16,163
- Hey! Hey, look at
this, another button.

79
00:03:16,163 --> 00:03:19,267
- I never noticed
that before. Hello?

80
00:03:27,675 --> 00:03:29,943
- Oh, hi Mike. I'm sorry.

81
00:03:29,943 --> 00:03:32,547
I should have told you we
were moving the castle.

82
00:03:32,547 --> 00:03:35,817
I didn't mean to
leave you home alone.

83
00:03:37,485 --> 00:03:39,287
Well, anyway, we had to.

84
00:03:39,287 --> 00:03:41,022
I finally got sick of paying

85
00:03:41,022 --> 00:03:44,325
50 bucks a year for
my monkey license.

86
00:03:44,325 --> 00:03:46,193
- Where do you want
the silverware?

87
00:03:46,193 --> 00:03:49,797
- Well, in the kitchen
where it always goes.

88
00:03:49,797 --> 00:03:50,632
50 bucks!

89
00:03:51,798 --> 00:03:53,668
I'm not gonna pay the
government 50 bucks

90
00:03:53,668 --> 00:03:56,637
for the privilege
of owning a monkey.

91
00:03:56,637 --> 00:03:59,440
How much do you pay for
your little things up there?

92
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:01,242
- Well, not that much.

93
00:04:02,677 --> 00:04:06,013
- Exactly. So anyway, we're
living in a much better place.

94
00:04:06,013 --> 00:04:08,983
It's quieter, frankly
it's a better neighborhood

95
00:04:08,983 --> 00:04:13,988
and they only charge 10 bucks
a year for the monkey license.

96
00:04:14,722 --> 00:04:15,957
Pretty shrewd, huh?

97
00:04:15,957 --> 00:04:19,093
- It's a nice one
too. Look, it's red.

98
00:04:19,093 --> 00:04:20,962
- Wow. Real neat.

99
00:04:20,962 --> 00:04:25,533
It does seem like kind of a
commotion just to save the $40.

100
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:26,633
But you know.

101
00:04:27,768 --> 00:04:30,103
- Oh no, Mike, it
only cost 2.3 million

102
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:31,905
to move the castle,
so it'll pay off

103
00:04:31,905 --> 00:04:36,510
in about 3,512 years, assuming
2% inflation each year.

104
00:04:36,510 --> 00:04:39,080
So you see how much
sense it makes...

105
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:40,315
- Well, maybe if you'd moved it

106
00:04:40,315 --> 00:04:42,083
with that big deal
brain of yours.

107
00:04:42,083 --> 00:04:44,185
- I'm not that
omnipotent, Pearl.

108
00:04:44,185 --> 00:04:45,720
And besides, we
packed everything up,

109
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:48,155
moved the castle here
only to unpack it

110
00:04:48,155 --> 00:04:49,823
and put it back again
in the same places.

111
00:04:49,823 --> 00:04:51,392
I mean, why?

112
00:04:51,392 --> 00:04:53,762
- Oh, I actually have a
pretty good reason for that.

113
00:04:53,762 --> 00:04:54,662
It's because.

114
00:04:54,662 --> 00:04:57,665
(Brain Guy groaning)

115
00:04:57,665 --> 00:04:59,167
- Oh, it's real
official too, look.

116
00:04:59,167 --> 00:05:03,403
"For control of parasite and
disease-riddled smelly apes."

117
00:05:03,403 --> 00:05:04,338
That's me. (laughs)

118
00:05:04,338 --> 00:05:06,407
- Go lay down, Bobo, lay down.

119
00:05:06,407 --> 00:05:07,875
As for you up there.

120
00:05:07,875 --> 00:05:09,543
- Oh, I'd imagine that
what with all the moving,

121
00:05:09,543 --> 00:05:12,247
you don't even have time for
a movie for us today, do ya?

122
00:05:12,247 --> 00:05:13,682
Huh, huh, huh?

123
00:05:13,682 --> 00:05:15,650
- Yeah. Right. Oh, no movie.

124
00:05:15,650 --> 00:05:17,952
Oh, except for this one.

125
00:05:17,952 --> 00:05:20,287
And it's a really bad movie.

126
00:05:20,287 --> 00:05:21,788
It's called "Horrors
of Spider Island."

127
00:05:21,788 --> 00:05:22,790
I hope that's okay.

128
00:05:22,790 --> 00:05:25,192
(Bobo barking)

129
00:05:25,192 --> 00:05:27,128
- Real peaceful in the
new neighborhood too.

130
00:05:27,128 --> 00:05:27,962
- Hey, no!

131
00:05:29,397 --> 00:05:32,533
(Bobo barking)

132
00:05:32,533 --> 00:05:33,968
(bots barking)
(alarms blaring)

133
00:05:33,968 --> 00:05:36,870
- Oh no, not the chain
bark, and we got movie sign!

134
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:38,038
Come on.

135
00:05:38,038 --> 00:05:42,910
(mechanical whirring)
(doors opening)

136
00:05:49,283 --> 00:05:51,018
- [Narrator] Horrors
of Spider Island!

137
00:05:51,018 --> 00:05:54,122
- [Mike] Give us a
chance to sit down.

138
00:05:54,122 --> 00:05:56,690
(sultry music)

139
00:05:58,092 --> 00:06:02,163
- [Crow] It's an anagram
for "Abrabra Navelnite."

140
00:06:03,597 --> 00:06:07,135
- [Tom] Temple Foster, where
they worship Australian beer.

141
00:06:07,135 --> 00:06:09,503
- [Crow] Hey, they're
playing make-out music, Mike.

142
00:06:09,503 --> 00:06:10,505
Whaddya say?

143
00:06:16,910 --> 00:06:18,847
- [Mike] Too bad we can't
grab this movie with a tissue

144
00:06:18,847 --> 00:06:22,617
and crumple it and flush
it down the toilet.

145
00:06:24,852 --> 00:06:26,087
- [Tom] Pacemaker.

146
00:06:26,087 --> 00:06:27,322
Ironically, they used a
lot of microwave ovens

147
00:06:27,322 --> 00:06:30,257
and metal detectors
during this movie.

148
00:06:35,062 --> 00:06:36,363
(upbeat music)

149
00:06:36,363 --> 00:06:40,468
- [Crow] Spider Island,
home to the stars.

150
00:06:40,468 --> 00:06:41,768
- [Mike] This is
back when every car

151
00:06:41,768 --> 00:06:45,105
was filled with a
private investigator.

152
00:06:47,342 --> 00:06:51,845
- [Tom] Boy, Spider
Island's all built up now.

153
00:06:51,845 --> 00:06:55,583
- [Crow] Hey, that guy
took his boat on land.

154
00:06:56,550 --> 00:06:59,053
(Servo humming along with music)

155
00:06:59,053 --> 00:07:01,322
♪ Parallel parking,
parallel parking ♪

156
00:07:01,322 --> 00:07:04,492
♪ Park park p-p-park. ♪

157
00:07:04,492 --> 00:07:07,995
- [Crow] It's a dames
and broads audition.

158
00:07:14,835 --> 00:07:19,307
- [Mike] Hey, nice office
for an enlisted man.

159
00:07:19,307 --> 00:07:23,010
- Here's Singapore, in
the South of Malaya.

160
00:07:23,010 --> 00:07:26,213
Population,
approximately 550,000.

161
00:07:26,213 --> 00:07:30,383
(indistinct) ship building,
important seaport.

162
00:07:30,383 --> 00:07:33,653
- Doesn't it say anything
about the 32 nightclubs there?

163
00:07:33,653 --> 00:07:36,823
- Have you already
worked down in Singapore?

164
00:07:36,823 --> 00:07:38,058
- Not to work.

165
00:07:38,058 --> 00:07:40,427
However, I once had a
friend an oil sheik.

166
00:07:40,427 --> 00:07:42,230
He took me with him down there.

167
00:07:42,230 --> 00:07:44,398
He was quite a guy.

168
00:07:44,398 --> 00:07:45,533
- Those are the guys that

169
00:07:45,533 --> 00:07:47,502
run around in
turbans, aren't they?

170
00:07:47,502 --> 00:07:49,503
- Listen honey, when they
take those turbans off,

171
00:07:49,503 --> 00:07:51,105
they're just like any other man.

172
00:07:51,105 --> 00:07:52,138
- [Crow] Turban-less.

173
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:53,307
- Got a light?

174
00:07:57,345 --> 00:07:59,313
- [Tom] Lucky sign.

175
00:07:59,313 --> 00:08:01,782
- Looking forward to
going to Singapore?

176
00:08:01,782 --> 00:08:03,617
- I don't really
care where I dance,

177
00:08:03,617 --> 00:08:05,787
as long as the pay's good.

178
00:08:09,623 --> 00:08:11,825
- [Mike] I'm Bob Box-body.

179
00:08:11,825 --> 00:08:13,427
- That's him there.

180
00:08:15,630 --> 00:08:18,798
- [Tom] I mind very
much if you smoke.

181
00:08:22,035 --> 00:08:25,238
- [Crow] Hey, quit doing your
Sharon Stone impersonation.

182
00:08:25,238 --> 00:08:26,073
- Hi.
- Hi.

183
00:08:28,208 --> 00:08:30,143
- I've already
been to Singapore.

184
00:08:30,143 --> 00:08:32,045
- And you look like it.

185
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:38,118
- [Mike] (chuckles) And I
said "You look like it."

186
00:08:38,652 --> 00:08:39,487
- Ah!

187
00:08:39,487 --> 00:08:40,555
- [Tom] Dr. Strangelove!

188
00:08:40,555 --> 00:08:42,323
- Hello Gary. Hi Georgia.

189
00:08:42,323 --> 00:08:44,192
You're looking
prettier every day.

190
00:08:44,192 --> 00:08:45,560
How in the world are you doing?

191
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:47,060
- Mike?
- Yeah?

192
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,397
- Have you told the girls
what this is all about?

193
00:08:49,397 --> 00:08:51,765
- Sure Gary, a tour
for a dancing troop.

194
00:08:51,765 --> 00:08:53,667
First engagement, Singapore.

195
00:08:53,667 --> 00:08:55,368
I have 12 of them
here to pick from.

196
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:56,603
- [Crow] Enjoy, Gary.

197
00:08:56,603 --> 00:08:57,872
- Okay Georgia.
Let the girls in.

198
00:08:57,872 --> 00:08:59,640
We don't have much time.

199
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:01,208
- All right if we start
now, Mr. Blackwood?

200
00:09:01,208 --> 00:09:02,175
- Of course.

201
00:09:03,310 --> 00:09:05,212
- Oh, but one at a time please.

202
00:09:05,212 --> 00:09:06,213
- Okay. May.

203
00:09:07,582 --> 00:09:10,383
- [Crow] We're looking for
someone who will sleep with us.

204
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:11,585
- Smile, would ya?

205
00:09:11,585 --> 00:09:12,687
- How do you do?

206
00:09:12,687 --> 00:09:14,155
- That's Mr.
Webster, the manager.

207
00:09:14,155 --> 00:09:17,358
And this is May, she's
the finest dancer in town.

208
00:09:17,358 --> 00:09:18,358
- [Tom] See?

209
00:09:19,227 --> 00:09:20,662
- What was your last engagement?

210
00:09:20,662 --> 00:09:22,397
- With the Coquettes, one year.

211
00:09:22,397 --> 00:09:23,630
- One of the finest.

212
00:09:23,630 --> 00:09:24,632
- Hmm. Legs?

213
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:27,033
- Pardon me?

214
00:09:27,033 --> 00:09:28,568
- Mr. Webster would like
to look at your legs.

215
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:29,503
- Oh, sure.

216
00:09:31,572 --> 00:09:32,573
- [Mike] Suppress
it, suppress it.

217
00:09:32,573 --> 00:09:33,573
- Thank you. You're hired.

218
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:34,708
Please wait outside.

219
00:09:34,708 --> 00:09:36,110
- Oh, thank you.

220
00:09:39,913 --> 00:09:41,948
- And this is Rhonda Hunter.

221
00:09:41,948 --> 00:09:43,150
- Dancer?

222
00:09:43,150 --> 00:09:46,987
- Not really, but I pick
things up real fast.

223
00:09:46,987 --> 00:09:47,822
- Hmm.

224
00:09:49,023 --> 00:09:51,292
- [Tom] Well, let's
see your clavicle.

225
00:09:51,292 --> 00:09:52,927
- Thank you, we're
looking for dancers,

226
00:09:52,927 --> 00:09:54,995
- But what's that got
to do with Singapore?

227
00:09:54,995 --> 00:09:56,497
- Come on, honey,
don't hold us up.

228
00:09:56,497 --> 00:09:59,000
- [Crow] This is how Ms.
magazine does its hiring.

229
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,600
- Babs?

230
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:03,003
- [Mike] Babs played
fullback for the Lions.

231
00:10:03,003 --> 00:10:04,272
- This is Babs.

232
00:10:04,272 --> 00:10:06,540
Her legs are worth
their weight in gold.

233
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:08,742
- Can those golden
legs also dance?

234
00:10:08,742 --> 00:10:11,578
- I was a solo dancer
in the Apollo variety.

235
00:10:11,578 --> 00:10:13,982
- And why did you leave there?

236
00:10:13,982 --> 00:10:15,650
- Oh, the boss
really went for her,

237
00:10:15,650 --> 00:10:18,252
but his wife thought otherwise.

238
00:10:19,387 --> 00:10:20,955
- [Crow] There it is again.

239
00:10:20,955 --> 00:10:22,623
- All right, you
can work with us

240
00:10:22,623 --> 00:10:24,525
as long as you don't
have any affairs.

241
00:10:24,525 --> 00:10:26,827
Mr. Webster doesn't
tolerate any fooling around.

242
00:10:26,827 --> 00:10:28,162
- [Mike] Yeah, that's cool.

243
00:10:28,162 --> 00:10:30,497
- I had all the boys I can take.

244
00:10:30,497 --> 00:10:31,332
- Come on.

245
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:33,733
Carolyn?

246
00:10:33,733 --> 00:10:35,837
- [Tom] Is this the
Ensure auditions?

247
00:10:35,837 --> 00:10:38,038
- This little one's from
the National Ballet.

248
00:10:38,038 --> 00:10:39,640
- Could you dance a
little bit for us?

249
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,242
- Glad to, would you
put that on for me?

250
00:10:41,242 --> 00:10:43,010
- Sure. Let's have a look.

251
00:10:43,010 --> 00:10:44,112
- [Crow] But none of
that modern stuff,

252
00:10:44,112 --> 00:10:46,080
