00:23:13,860 --> 00:23:16,362
- [Crow] It's a giant
sea donut, we're saved!

499
00:23:16,362 --> 00:23:17,863
Oh, it's the raft.

500
00:23:19,265 --> 00:23:21,400
(Servo humming)

501
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:26,405
(mechanical whirring)
(doors closing)

502
00:23:33,713 --> 00:23:36,048
(grunting)

503
00:23:36,048 --> 00:23:38,352
- Mike, what the
hell are you doing?

504
00:23:38,352 --> 00:23:41,187
- Trying to extricate
myself from this giant web.

505
00:23:41,187 --> 00:23:42,188
- Well be careful will ya,

506
00:23:42,188 --> 00:23:43,490
and don't disturb the giant fly.

507
00:23:43,490 --> 00:23:45,625
That's our lunch.

508
00:23:45,625 --> 00:23:47,127
- Okay, you know, I'm
not going to go into

509
00:23:47,127 --> 00:23:49,728
how you made a giant web,
I just want to know why?

510
00:23:49,728 --> 00:23:51,430
- Well, I think the more
important question is

511
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:53,700
what possessed you to leap
blindly across the bridge

512
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:55,902
and get caught in
the first place?

513
00:23:55,902 --> 00:23:59,005
Do you routinely spring out
of the theater like a gazelle?

514
00:23:59,005 --> 00:24:01,942
- Crow, how do I get outta here?

515
00:24:01,942 --> 00:24:03,377
- Good question.

516
00:24:03,377 --> 00:24:05,945
Can you excrete oily web-proof
spittle from your mouth?

517
00:24:05,945 --> 00:24:07,880
- Uh, yeah. I think so.

518
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:09,315
Hang on, let me get a quick-

519
00:24:09,315 --> 00:24:10,450
Of course I can't.

520
00:24:10,450 --> 00:24:11,685
- Hey, hey.

521
00:24:11,685 --> 00:24:12,918
I'm not the one who
sprinted headlong

522
00:24:12,918 --> 00:24:15,922
into a large and
very obvious web.

523
00:24:15,922 --> 00:24:18,492
- Here's some roasted
potato bug and dip.

524
00:24:18,492 --> 00:24:21,728
This web's going to have
us eatin' like kings.

525
00:24:21,728 --> 00:24:23,197
Mike, what the
hell are you doing?

526
00:24:23,197 --> 00:24:24,730
- Apparently he
was pogo sticking

527
00:24:24,730 --> 00:24:26,733
blindfolded across the bridge.

528
00:24:26,733 --> 00:24:28,335
- too bad. Let's eat.

529
00:24:28,335 --> 00:24:29,402
I had no idea there were so many

530
00:24:29,402 --> 00:24:31,270
giant insects on the satellite.

531
00:24:31,270 --> 00:24:33,840
- I had no idea they'd
be so delicious.

532
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:35,042
- Hey, hey.

533
00:24:35,042 --> 00:24:37,177
Now there's a giant
spider, help me.

534
00:24:37,177 --> 00:24:38,612
- That's a pretty
lame impression

535
00:24:38,612 --> 00:24:40,613
of David Hedison
in "The Fly," Mike.

536
00:24:40,613 --> 00:24:42,048
- Come on Crow, the
giant mantis fingers

537
00:24:42,048 --> 00:24:43,450
are bubbling hot with cheese.

538
00:24:43,450 --> 00:24:45,718
- Yummy! See ya, Mike.

539
00:24:45,718 --> 00:24:48,588
- Well, I'm dead and
we'll be right back.

540
00:24:48,588 --> 00:24:49,422
Hey!

541
00:24:50,290 --> 00:24:53,860
(instrumental theme music)

542
00:24:56,395 --> 00:24:58,265
(sultry saxophone music)

543
00:24:58,265 --> 00:25:01,100
- [Mike] Corn's
looking good here.

544
00:25:02,268 --> 00:25:05,872
(Tom hums along with music)

545
00:25:06,973 --> 00:25:09,542
- [Crow] And
Hedonism II is born.

546
00:25:10,643 --> 00:25:12,945
- [Tom] I've
enslaved the natives.

547
00:25:12,945 --> 00:25:14,180
- Water!

548
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:17,283
- [Crow] That's what
dried soup mix needs.

549
00:25:21,487 --> 00:25:25,725
- [Mike] Ah, the girls
deserve to see my thickness.

550
00:25:27,360 --> 00:25:30,930
- [Crow] Do we
have to watch this?

551
00:25:30,930 --> 00:25:33,367
- Water, water, water, water!

552
00:25:34,267 --> 00:25:36,837
Come on, come on, come on.

553
00:25:36,837 --> 00:25:39,738
(women exclaiming)

554
00:25:51,317 --> 00:25:53,185
- Fresh drinking water.

555
00:25:53,185 --> 00:25:57,590
- [Tom] The best way to get
it is to lick it off my chest.

556
00:25:57,590 --> 00:25:58,758
- Spring water.

557
00:25:58,758 --> 00:26:01,093
- [Mike] The graceful,
nimble dancers.

558
00:26:01,093 --> 00:26:02,628
(women exclaiming)

559
00:26:02,628 --> 00:26:05,065
- [Crow] I am one lucky bastard.

560
00:26:05,065 --> 00:26:07,400
- [Tom] Oh, I hope this
water isn't fattening.

561
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:11,570
- Oh, is there anything
more wonderful than water?

562
00:26:13,138 --> 00:26:15,442
- Okay, girls. That's enough.

563
00:26:15,442 --> 00:26:17,010
Let's go and have a look around.

564
00:26:17,010 --> 00:26:19,445
Come on, come on, come on.

565
00:26:19,445 --> 00:26:21,547
Ready? Let's go.

566
00:26:21,547 --> 00:26:23,883
- [Mike] But I'm severely
dehydrated, can I drink more?

567
00:26:23,883 --> 00:26:27,120
- [Crow] No, we must get moving.

568
00:26:27,120 --> 00:26:28,522
- Feeling better now?

569
00:26:28,522 --> 00:26:30,423
Don't lag behind.

570
00:26:30,423 --> 00:26:31,658
- [Mike] Let's go visit

571
00:26:31,658 --> 00:26:34,227
Brooke Shields and
Christopher Atkins.

572
00:26:34,227 --> 00:26:35,962
- Heels are too high for here.

573
00:26:35,962 --> 00:26:37,363
- Hey, here's your scarf.

574
00:26:37,363 --> 00:26:38,932
- Oh, keep it.

575
00:26:38,932 --> 00:26:39,765
- Coming?

576
00:26:41,167 --> 00:26:44,270
- [Tom] What, he's not going
to carry us this time? (scoffs)

577
00:26:44,270 --> 00:26:47,773
- [Mike] Um, schlemiel
schlimazel, anyone?

578
00:26:51,745 --> 00:26:52,678
- Ow

579
00:26:52,678 --> 00:26:55,415
- [Crow] My tender man skin.

580
00:26:55,415 --> 00:26:56,683
- Careful, girls.

581
00:26:56,683 --> 00:26:59,652
- [Tom] Don't let my raw
sexuality overwhelm you.

582
00:26:59,652 --> 00:27:03,390
(all imitate women mumbling)

583
00:27:06,827 --> 00:27:08,728
- What a strange sight.

584
00:27:10,363 --> 00:27:11,798
- Well, let's keep going.

585
00:27:11,798 --> 00:27:15,102
- [Mike] I refuse to
comment on what you said.

586
00:27:15,102 --> 00:27:18,505
- [Crow] Hot, muddy
foreign chick action.

587
00:27:23,042 --> 00:27:24,843
- Ouch, my shoe.

588
00:27:24,843 --> 00:27:28,180
- [Mike] "Feels like
a sneaker," my ass.

589
00:27:30,917 --> 00:27:33,453
- Gary, look what I just found.

590
00:27:33,453 --> 00:27:34,787
- [Tom] A stick!

591
00:27:36,222 --> 00:27:39,758
- A hammer. There must be
someone on this island.

592
00:27:39,758 --> 00:27:42,028
A hammer with a long handle.

593
00:27:42,028 --> 00:27:43,195
- [Crow] That's me.

594
00:27:43,195 --> 00:27:44,397
- It must be for the purpose

595
00:27:44,397 --> 00:27:46,733
of excavating some
sort of metal.

596
00:27:46,733 --> 00:27:48,768
Most probably uranium.

597
00:27:48,768 --> 00:27:50,403
- Can you eat that?

598
00:27:50,403 --> 00:27:52,138
- Yeah, you can try it.

599
00:27:52,138 --> 00:27:54,173
Come on. Let's go and find out.

600
00:27:54,173 --> 00:27:57,243
- [Mike] Be sure and murmur
and coo some more too.

601
00:27:57,243 --> 00:27:58,310
Uh-huh, good.

602
00:27:59,312 --> 00:28:00,513
Yeah. Keep it up now.

603
00:28:00,513 --> 00:28:03,483
That's it. Hey Susie,
I don't hear you.

604
00:28:05,618 --> 00:28:08,688
(women murmuring)

605
00:28:08,688 --> 00:28:09,922
- [Crow] And people
complain that there

606
00:28:09,922 --> 00:28:12,692
aren't any strong
roles for women.

607
00:28:13,693 --> 00:28:14,860
- Come on, hurry up.

608
00:28:14,860 --> 00:28:16,195
Look, come here.

609
00:28:16,195 --> 00:28:17,830
- [Mike] Duck, swim.

610
00:28:17,830 --> 00:28:19,165
- Look, a cabin!

611
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:22,435
- [Tom] The
Leatherface residence.

612
00:28:22,435 --> 00:28:25,638
(women murmuring happily)

613
00:28:25,638 --> 00:28:27,040
- [Crow] I call
the bathroom first!

614
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:29,308
- [Mike] No, me.
- I get it.

615
00:28:29,308 --> 00:28:31,745
(screaming)

616
00:28:31,745 --> 00:28:34,080
- [Mike] Charlotte's
killing spree.

617
00:28:34,080 --> 00:28:35,315
- Oooh...

618
00:28:35,315 --> 00:28:36,382
- [Crow] It's gorgeous.

619
00:28:36,382 --> 00:28:38,317
- Let's get outta here.

620
00:28:39,818 --> 00:28:42,788
- [Mike] All right, now watch
how a man screams in horror.

621
00:28:42,788 --> 00:28:44,290
(dramatic music)

622
00:28:44,290 --> 00:28:47,293
- [Tom] He was caught in the
middle of a cheerleading move.

623
00:28:47,293 --> 00:28:50,363
- A dead man, in a huge web.

624
00:28:50,363 --> 00:28:54,867
- [Mike] Oh, I was
looking at the wallpaper.

625
00:28:54,867 --> 00:28:59,372
- [Crow] Murmur, murmur,
slightly more intense murmur.

626
00:29:03,108 --> 00:29:05,178
- [Tom] We've got
spirit, yes we do.

627
00:29:05,178 --> 00:29:08,080
We've got spirit,
how 'bout... (groans)

628
00:29:08,080 --> 00:29:09,782
- [Crow] MRxL.

629
00:29:09,782 --> 00:29:11,350
Get rid of the dead guy,
turn on the LP tanks,

630
00:29:11,350 --> 00:29:14,287
put out the dog,
we're ready to go.

631
00:29:16,488 --> 00:29:19,325
- [Mike] Can I be
in your cluster?

632
00:29:20,360 --> 00:29:21,360
- Hey there!

633
00:29:24,363 --> 00:29:25,865
Come on.

634
00:29:25,865 --> 00:29:30,002
- [Crow] She was appointed
acting Gary in his absence.

635
00:29:31,570 --> 00:29:35,175
- [Tom] Damn, I was just
about to pinch her tush.

636
00:29:35,175 --> 00:29:36,375
- The poor professor.

637
00:29:36,375 --> 00:29:38,745
When he made the last
entry in the diary,

638
00:29:38,745 --> 00:29:41,948
he didn't know how
horribly he would die.

639
00:29:41,948 --> 00:29:45,117
- Well, the discovery
of the uranium deposits

640
00:29:45,117 --> 00:29:47,687
didn't help him
any, even if it does

641
00:29:47,687 --> 00:29:49,588
represent a tremendous fortune.

642
00:29:49,588 --> 00:29:51,157
- [Crow] Well, gotta
tighten my shirt.

643
00:29:51,157 --> 00:29:52,658
- We must keep it from the girls

644
00:29:52,658 --> 00:29:55,395
that Professor Green had
a premonition of his fate.

645
00:29:55,395 --> 00:29:57,963
- You see here in
the last paragraph,

646
00:29:57,963 --> 00:30:01,600
he says he thought something
terrible was going to happen.

647
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:04,170
He just felt the danger.

648
00:30:04,170 --> 00:30:07,340
- I wonder where that
peculiar hissing came from

649
00:30:07,340 --> 00:30:08,508
that he always heard.

650
00:30:08,508 --> 00:30:09,675
- [Tom] The audience.

651
00:30:09,675 --> 00:30:11,377
- Oh Gary, I'm terribly scared.

652
00:30:11,377 --> 00:30:13,312
I'm so afraid.

653
00:30:13,312 --> 00:30:14,413
- Don't worry, Georgia.

654
00:30:14,413 --> 00:30:15,882
- Oh, okay. I won't, thanks.

655
00:30:15,882 --> 00:30:19,352
- As long as I'm around,
nothing will happen to you.

656
00:30:19,352 --> 00:30:21,020
I promise.

657
00:30:21,020 --> 00:30:23,222
- [Crow] Look into my nose now.

658
00:30:23,222 --> 00:30:24,057
- Hi, Georgia.

659
00:30:24,057 --> 00:30:25,225
- I'm hungry.

660
00:30:25,225 --> 00:30:26,525
- I've made something
for you to eat.

661
00:30:26,525 --> 00:30:28,193
Luckily, there were
some canned goods here.

662
00:30:28,193 --> 00:30:32,698
- [Tom] Wardrobe, we have
a birth scene problem.

663
00:30:32,698 --> 00:30:34,667
- It must have been a
really gigantic spider

664
00:30:34,667 --> 00:30:37,270
to be able to spin
such a huge web.

665
00:30:37,270 --> 00:30:38,705
Maybe there are more of them.

666
00:30:38,705 --> 00:30:42,575
- But a bite like that couldn't
have come from a spider.

667
00:30:42,575 --> 00:30:43,943
- Aren't you at all afraid?

668
00:30:43,943 --> 00:30:47,347
- Afraid? I can't
change anything.

669
00:30:47,347 --> 00:30:49,948
- I'm terribly afraid something
awful is going to happen.

670
00:30:49,948 --> 00:30:52,152
- [Mike] Unlike the plane crash.

671
00:30:52,152 --> 00:30:53,587
- (gasps) Look!

672
00:30:53,587 --> 00:30:56,488
- [Tom] It's our
friend who just left.

673
00:30:56,488 --> 00:30:58,625
- We found the professor's
trunk full of stuff.

674
00:30:58,625 --> 00:30:59,858
They'll certainly be useful.

675
00:30:59,858 --> 00:31:01,727
- [Crow] Boxer
shorts and his truss.

676
00:31:01,727 --> 00:31:04,930
- One, four, five, six,
seven, eight. Okay.

677
00:31:04,930 --> 00:31:07,900
- [Tom] We can sell this
stuff to the others.

678
00:31:07,900 --> 00:31:09,702
- If we divide the
provisions up carefully,

679
00:31:09,702 --> 00:31:12,238
they should last for a month.

680
00:31:12,238 --> 00:31:14,373
- What did you say
Georgia, a month?

681
00:31:14,373 --> 00:31:17,543
Do you really think I'll
be here a whole month?

682
00:31:17,543 --> 00:31:18,477
- I don't know.

683
00:31:18,477 --> 00:31:19,678
- [Crow] Thank you, Georgia.

684
00:31:19,678 --> 00:31:21,447
- We have to go tomorrow
to the highest cliff

685
00:31:21,447 --> 00:31:25,652
and light a smoke signal to
try and attract the ship.

686
00:31:25,652 --> 00:31:26,552
10, 11, 12.

687
00:31:28,220 --> 00:31:30,590
- [Mike] Hey, they brought
Virginia Graham along.

688
00:31:30,590 --> 00:31:31,557
- Give me that shirt!

689
00:31:31,557 --> 00:31:32,392
- No, it belongs to me.

690
00:31:32,392 --> 00:31:33,593
After all, I found it.

691
00:31:33,593 --> 00:31:34,860
- But my dress is in
worse shape than yours.

692
00:31:34,860 --> 00:31:36,562
- No, I want to have it.

693
00:31:36,562 --> 00:31:37,397
Give it to me.

694
00:31:37,397 --> 00:31:39,598
(women yelling)

695
00:31:39,598 --> 00:31:41,633
- Stop that fighting.
Give me that shirt.

696
00:31:41,633 --> 00:31:43,368
- [Crow] You both get no shirts.

697
00:31:43,368 --> 00:31:44,337
- Georgia.

698
00:31:44,337 --> 00:31:46,138
- [Tom] Cook this for dinner.

699
00:31:46,138 --> 00:31:47,907
- Thanks, Gary.

700
00:31:47,907 --> 00:31:49,308
- I suppose we
could have guessed

701
00:31:49,308 --> 00:31:50,877
that Georgia would
be getting it.

702
00:31:50,877 --> 00:31:53,212
- [Crow] That sheer fabric
would make a good shirt.

703
00:31:53,212 --> 00:31:55,382
- Haven't you ever noticed
that Gary pampers her?

704
00:31:55,382 --> 00:31:56,348
- What's this?

705
00:31:56,348 --> 00:31:57,817
Where did you get the pullover?

706
00:31:57,817 --> 00:32:01,687
- I found it here, if you
don't have anything against it.

707
00:32:01,687 --> 00:32:04,690
- Now stop it or I'll
take care of both of you.

708
00:32:04,690 --> 00:32:06,825
Give me something to drink.

709
00:32:06,825 --> 00:32:08,127
- [Tom] Rice vinegar's
fine, thanks.

710
00:32:08,127 --> 00:32:09,062
- Take it easy, Gary.

711
00:32:09,062 --> 00:32:11,030
We're all a little nervous.

712
00:32:11,030 --> 00:32:13,165
It's really no wonder.

713
00:32:13,165 --> 00:32:16,335
- Don't you think I'd rather
be in a bar in Singapore

714
00:32:16,335 --> 00:32:19,238
with a nice cold
drink, than to be on

715
00:32:19,238 --> 00:32:20,907
this godforsaken place?

716
00:32:20,907 --> 00:32:23,508
- [Mike] With eight hot babes?

717
00:32:23,508 --> 00:32:25,578
- Drinking this horrible stuff?

718
00:32:25,578 --> 00:32:27,113
- [Tom] How-er-able?

719
00:32:27,113 --> 00:32:30,717
(instrumental theme music)

720
00:32:35,087 --> 00:32:36,088
- Darn heat.

721
00:32:39,025 --> 00:32:40,258
(cup clattering)

722
00:32:40,258 --> 00:32:41,160
- [Crow] It didn't
stay in the air.

723
00:32:41,160 --> 00:32:42,095
- Cut it out, will ya?

724
00:32:42,095 --> 00:32:43,528
And stop making so much noise.

725
00:32:43,528 --> 00:32:45,197
- If you don't like it,
you can do the dishes.

726
00:32:45,197 --> 00:32:48,167
Or do you think I'm doing
this for my own pleasure?

727
00:32:48,167 --> 00:32:50,302
- Stop blowing your top
and dry up, will ya?

728
00:32:50,302 --> 00:32:54,773
- [Mike] I can't wait
til the spiders eat you.

729
00:32:54,773 --> 00:32:56,608
- (sighing) I simply can't stand

730
00:32:56,608 --> 00:32:58,510
this frightful heat any longer.

731
00:32:58,510 --> 00:33:02,448
- [Tom] Ah, the movie
reveals its true purpose.

732
00:33:05,385 --> 00:33:08,220
- How about throwing your
dirty blouse someplace else?

733
00:33:08,220 --> 00:33:09,422
I want sleep

734
00:33:09,422 --> 00:33:11,690
- [Crow] Excuse me, Charro?

735
00:33:13,125 --> 00:33:18,130
- [Mike] Hey, I have some
Slim Fast bars, we're saved.

736
00:33:19,332 --> 00:33:21,467
- [Tom] So anyone
wanna catfight or?

737
00:33:21,467 --> 00:33:23,402
- I sure hope you don't
lose your lipstick.

738
00:33:23,402 --> 00:33:26,305
You'd hardly be able to get
along on this Island without it.

739
00:33:26,305 --> 00:33:30,977
- [Crow] Her accent changed
three times in one sentence.

740
00:33:32,512 --> 00:33:34,747
(knocking)

741
00:33:36,048 --> 00:33:38,483
- It's about time.
Now I'll shower.

742
00:33:38,483 --> 00:33:39,585
Give it here.

743
00:33:40,453 --> 00:33:42,422
- Come on, come on, girls.

744
00:33:42,422 --> 00:33:43,355
Let's go to sleep.

745
00:33:43,355 --> 00:33:44,490
- I'm going to sleep outside.

746
00:33:44,490 --> 00:33:45,323
- Me too.

747
00:33:48,127 --> 00:33:50,028
- Goodnight.
- Goodnight, Kate.

748
